1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jakob Jakobsen Foss was born on the farm Verpelstad (1) in Evanger, Hordaland in 1859 and moved to Hyllestad, Sogn in 1873 when his father bought the farm Øvre Foss (2) ("''uppermost waterfall''").
2 CONT
2 CONT Verpelstad is located along the railroad between Bergen and Voss that opened in 1883 (4). When agreement was reached as to the right-of-way for the railway line in 1873 it became clare that the railroad would run diirectly past Ve
2 CONC rpelstad. The same year Jakobs father moved his family from Verpelstad to Øvre Foss to protect his five daughters from roughneck railroad workers (''rallare'') that would soon move into the area. Verpelstad later functioned as a r
2 CONC ailway station.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakob immigrated from Øvre Foss, Hyllestad to the United States in 1882 at age 23, onboard a ''Dominion Line'' ship sailing from Bergen 21/4/1882 (4). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) 60°37'2.66"N 5°52'59.78"E http://www.vaksdalhistorielag.org/wiki/index.php?title=Verpelstad
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) 61° 8'55.82"N 5°21'9.31"E
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voss_Line
2 CONT
2 CONT (4) http://digitalarkivet.no/cgi-win/webcens.exe?slag=visbase&filnamn=0214EMIG&personpostnr=22&merk=22
2 CONT
2 CONT Verpelstad farm: http://nesthus.net/photo/48531
2 CONT
2 CONT Øvre Foss farm: http://www.fylkesarkiv.no/foto/detalj?http://www.sffarkiv.no/sffbasar/default.asp?p=result&ptype=single&db=dbfoto&sql=sfffoto%20=%20%27SFFf-100542.262078%27
2 CONT
2 CONT Old stone bridge downstream from the waterfall (''foss'') at Øvre Foss farm: http://www.sffarkiv.no/samsok3/Artikkel/1241/FossBruIHyllestad-EitVakkertKulturminneHyllestadKristin?instruks::20:1:ResultSimple:Artikkel
