1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Myrtle Vivian was born February 6, 1899 in Iowa to Andrew and Emily (Erickson) Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Education was important to her family, and she completed 2 years of college. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In about 1922, she married a young World War veteran with hazel eyes and brown hair named Joseph Earl Tamisiea. After the war, he completed 2 more years of college, and worked in the hardware business. They lived in Missouri Valle
2 CONC y, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1930, the family was living at 621 Superior, Missouri Valley. The 1930 US Census lists: J. Earl, 31, head, salesman hardware store, b. IA Myrtle V., 31, wife, b. IA Vivian M., 6, daughter, b. IA Barbara L.,1, daughter, b. IA
2 CONT
2 CONT From at least 1935 to 1940, the family lived at 621 E. Michigan, Missouri Valley, Iowa. The 1940 US Census lists: Earl, 41, head, 3 yrs college, proprietor & ___ of an implement hardware company, b. IA Myrtle, 41, wife, 2 yrs coll
2 CONC ege, b. IA Vivian, 16, daughter, b. IA Barbara, 11, daughter, b. IA Maureen, 7, daughter, b. IA
