1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "I Remember" by Grannie Annie Larson. I have put my own comments are starred
2 CONT
2 CONT This old man* put two of his nephews (NOTE: one brother and a nephew)  through medical school in Chicago**. David married, then he died (just short of graduation) and left a widow and four children. A good grandmother took them al
2 CONC l in, they were related to the Drugsvolds**** out by Scarville.
2 CONT
2 CONT * she is referring to Guleik Gullickson, who was later known as Dr. Gilbert Herm and practiced in Lake Mills, Iowa.
2 CONT ** Hanemann Medical College of Chicago 
2 CONT *** David is Gilbert's brother and was married in 1890 in Forest City , Iowa.
2 CONT **** Anders Jonson Draugsvoll and Martha Gullickson. Martha is David and Gilbert's sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT *** His obituary was published in the Lake Mills Graphic after his death which was 29 Sep 1900.
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcript:  David C. Gullickson of Logan twp, and who was well known and had many friends in L.M. died Sun. last of typhoid fever aged 32 years and 6 months. The funeral services were held yesterday and the remains interred in Be
2 CONC thel cemetery. A number of Friends from L.M. were in attendance. Dave, as he was familiarly known, had been attending medical college for the past two or three years and had only one term left in which to complete the course. He w
2 CONC as a bright young man and his loss will be deeply felt by the community in which he has resided for years. He leaves a wife and four children to mourn his loss.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
