1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Buried Apr 16, 1924 Stone on grave
2 CONT
2 CONT Of interest: In the Carrot River Valley Lutheran Church cemetery record...they have Bernard Lofthus & Lloyd Lofthus in the same grave...South E G08...(both are babies..one belonged to Bernhardt Lofthus & one to Martin Lofthus ) bu
2 CONC t yet they say that Lloyd has a stone, but Bernard does not.. Then they have Helmer Lofthus buried in grave South E G09.
2 CONT
2 CONT If Bernard does not have a stone on his grave then I am assuming that he is most likely buried in South E G09...and somehow someone put a stone on his grave for Helmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT The church may not have noticed that they had 2 babies in one grave, so when 1 grave showed up with no one in it...they just assumed it must be Helmer...but the Carrot River Valley Lutheran Church was not built until 1909.  Karl H
2 CONC elmer Loftus is buried at the Melfort Creek Cemetery.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/124831759/lloyd-loftus Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 7 2020, 9:48:1
2 CONC 6 UTC''
