2 ADDR
1 FAMS @F6000000003889769423@
1 RFN geni:6000000003888343203
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 NOTE
2 CONT Esther Peterson, 85, of Highlandville
2 CONT Esther M. Peterson, 85, of Decorah, a former longtime owner of the Peterson Store in Highlandville, Iowa, died Friday, July 25, 2003, at the Barthell Eastern Star Nursing Home in Decorah.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born April 1, 1918, in Goldfield, Iowa, to Harry and Fern (Straight) Hanson. She was baptized and confirmed at the First Presbyterian Church in Monmouth, Ill. She graduated from the Monmouth High School and then the Burlin
2 CONC gton Business College in Burlington, Iowa. She worked for Brown, Lynch and Scott, and Banker’s Life in Monmouth.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct. 9, 1944, she married Myron Peterson in Monmouth. The couple operated the Peterson Store in Highlandville, rural Decorah, for 46 years. She retired in 1995. He died Aug. 15, 1986.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a resident at the Green Lea Manor Nursing Home in Mabel before moving to the Barthell Eastern Star Nursing Home in Decorah. She was a member of the Highland Lutheran Church in rural Spring Grove and the American Legion Pos
2 CONC t 299 Auxiliary, and enjoyed gardening and visiting.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by one son, Greg (Judy) Peterson of Bangor, Wis.; one daughter, Mary (Sverre) Dahl of Hesper, Iowa; seven grandchildren; four great-grandchildren; and a sister, Katie Cross of Galesburg, Ill. She was preceded in de
2 CONC ath by two sisters, Edith Yarde and Ellen Hanson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were Tuesday at the Highland Lutheran Church in rural Spring Grove with the Rev. David Andreae officiating. Burial was in the church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mengis Funeral Home in Mabel was in charge of arrangements.
1 NOTE
2 CONT Esther Hanson becomes bride of Cpl. Myron Peterson - Choosing the date of his parents wedding anniversary for the day of his marriage, Myron Peterson, Corporal in the Army of the United States and a veteran of the Southwest Pacifi
2 CONC c Campaign was united in marriage at 8 o'clock October 9, 1944 to Miss Esther Hanson, daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Harry Hanson, Decorah, Iowa.  The ceremony was performed at the First Lutheran Church, Decorah by the Pastor, Rev. H. R
2 CONC . Ekerburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Arthur Hanson served as her sister's matron of honor.  The bridesmaids were Miss Julia Frances Worrell and Miss Valborg Peterson.
2 CONT
2 CONT The bridgegroom was attended by his brother, Truman Peterson of Dorchester, Iowa.  The ushers were Pvt. Harlan Eleffson of Woodville, Wis., and Sgt. Earl Paulson of Racine, Wisconsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the ceremony a reception for guests was held in the church parlors.  Mrs. Harry Yarde, sister of the bride and Mrs. Harold St. Mary sister of the bridegroom presided at the serving table.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Peteson graduated from Monmouth High School and the Burlington, Iowa College of Commerce.  She just recently resigned her position in the offices of the Illinois Bankers Life Insurance Company.  She is a member of Monmouth Re
2 CONC bekah Lodge No. 128 and Beta Sigma Phi fraternity for business women.
2 CONT
2 CONT Corporal Peterson is the son of Mr. and Mrs. G. M. Peterson of Dorchester, Iowa and a graduate of Spring Grove High School.  He entered service with the armed forces in 1941 and served thirteen months with the infantry in the sout
2 CONC hwest Pacific before he was wounded and sent eventaully to Mayo General Hospital at Galesburg. After a short honeymoon spent in La Crosse, Wis. and Dorchester, Iowa, Cpl. and Mrs. Peterson will live in Galesburg, Illinois.
