1 NAME George William /Purtle/
2 GIVN George William
2 _MARNM Purtle
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 SEP 1927
2 ADDR
3 STAE MO
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 DEC 1962
2 ADDR
3 CITY Missouri Valley
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George was born September 7, 1927 in Missouri to Milton L. and Gladys F. Purtle.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1930, the family had moved to Belknap, in Pottawattamie County, Iowa (near Harrison County and near Council Bluffs), where his father managed a farm. Other neighbors told the census taker that they were farmers, but Milton said
2 CONC  he was a manager. The 1930 US Census lists:
2 CONT Milton L. Purtle, 27, head, b.MO, manager, farm
2 CONT Gladys F. Purtle, 26, wife, b.MO
2 CONT George W. Purtle, 2, son, b.MO
2 CONT
2 CONT Times were hard during the Depression. By 1935, George and his family had moved back to Missouri, and were living in Atchison County there. However, by 1940, George's father was farming at his own place, in Atchison County, Missou
2 CONC ri. Although Gladys had completed high school, Milton had to go to work on the farm after 6th grade. In 1940, George was in school, and had completed 5th grade. There was a new little sister, Bernice J., now 4 years old, who had b
2 CONC een born in Iowa. (Note: he had a baby sister who died in 1934, named Phyllis)
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 20, 1945, George had turned 18, and was hired by the Chicago and North Western railroad, to work as a laborer. 
